---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/ui/FAQAccordion.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/trust/TrustBar.astro';
import { faqSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import { TRADE_LANES } from '../../data/trade-lanes';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Trade Lanes', href: '/shipping' }];
const description =
  'FCL and air freight forwarding from any origin, with in-house customs, warehousing, and delivery. China and Vietnam are two lanes handled in depth below.';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Do you only ship from China and Vietnam?',
    answer:
      'No. Global Gate Logistics ships FCL and air cargo from any origin, not only the two lanes detailed on this page. Request a quote for your specific origin and destination.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between ocean and air freight for these lanes?',
    answer:
      'Ocean freight is almost always cheaper per kilogram for heavy cargo, while air freight is competitive for shipments under roughly 500 kilograms or when a delay would cost more than the freight itself. Ocean transit runs 14 to 38 days depending on the US coast; air transit runs 3 to 7 days door to door.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Trade Lanes" {description} pathname="/shipping" {breadcrumbs} schemas={[faqSchema(faqs)]}>
  <div class="bg-navy-900">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={breadcrumbs} />
    <div class="container-gg pb-12 pt-4 max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-white mb-4" style="font-size:clamp(2.25rem,5.5vw,3.75rem)">Trade Lanes</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-300">{description}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <TrustBar />

  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="container-gg max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="font-display text-navy-900 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Choosing ocean or air, and why the lane doesn't limit you</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-5">
        Ocean and air freight solve different problems, and the right one depends on what's actually being shipped. Ocean FCL and LCL is almost always cheaper per kilogram and remains the default for full container loads and bulkier LCL consolidations, with transit typically running 14 to 20 days to the US West Coast and 28 to 38 days to the US East Coast, including the Port of NY/NJ. Air freight is the better choice when a shipment is light relative to its value &mdash; generally under roughly 500 kilograms &mdash; or when the cost of waiting exceeds the cost of shipping; door-to-door air transit typically runs 3 to 7 days. Within ocean freight itself, FCL usually becomes cheaper per cubic meter once a shipment exceeds roughly 15 CBM, with LCL the more economical option below that threshold.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-5">
        China and Vietnam are the two lanes detailed below because they account for the largest share of the freight Global Gate Logistics moves today, but they are not the only origins served. FCL and air freight are handled for any origin or destination, using the same direct carrier service contracts, IATA membership, and in-house operations regardless of where a shipment starts.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Every lane runs through the same in-house pipeline rather than a chain of subcontracted vendors: ISF filing ahead of the 24-hour-before-loading deadline for ocean imports, customs entry and HTS classification filed by the same team that books the freight, and warehousing and drayage minutes from JFK and the Port of New York and New Jersey for final delivery. That single-team structure is what keeps a rate request, a customs question, and a delivery update all answered by one point of contact.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-gg py-16">
    <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {TRADE_LANES.map((lane) => (
        <li class="bg-white border border-slate-100 rounded-xl p-6 hover:border-amber-400 transition-colors">
          <a href={`/shipping/${lane.slug}`} class="block">
            <span class="font-display text-navy-900 font-bold text-lg block mb-2">{lane.name}</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-sm">{lane.tagline}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
  <CTABand />
  <FAQAccordion {faqs} heading="Trade lanes: common questions" />
</BaseLayout>
